# A0 optimizer, written in A0 (DESIGN.md 7a): the port of src/optimize.ts `optimizeFunction`
# (expand, pass, forwardAggregates, schedule, literal iterations), node for node what the
# TypeScript optimizer gives: same nodes in the same order, same operands, same ret, tools/
# selfhost-wasm.ts `a0IrCheck` compares them (and the literal iteration bound) on every function.
#
# One run optimizes ONE function (`ozone`, mode 7 of `emitwasmio`): a single A0 value, a fold
# state included, is at most 65536 words, and a function's operand table alone can fill that, so
# no run can hold a loop over functions. The driver runs the functions of a program in program
# order and feeds each run the optimized bodies it needs (src/optimize.ts `optimizedCallee`: an
# optimized body is a function of the callee's original body and its callees' optimized
# bodies). The driver only does bookkeeping: encoding, ordering, supplying requested bodies.
#
# Input words after the mode, in the layout of the checked tables of mode 2 (paged u32x128xN;
# word w at page w>>7): types (count, triples), tlist, functions (count, 7 words each: word 0
# is bit 0 "has a body" and literalIterations * 2, 1 the parameter count, 2 the first
# parameter in tlist, 3 the result type, 4 the first node, 5 the node count, 6 the packed ret
# kind * 2^28 + value, kind 5: the pair at operand slot value), nodes (count, 6 words each: 0,
# op, operand count, first operand slot, callee, predicate; callee and predicate are function
# indices), the node types, operand pairs (count, kind and value, kinds 1 node 2 parameter 3
# u32 4 bool), then for every function two summary words (node count; bit 0 all parameters
# scalar, 1 result scalar, 2 all node types scalar, 3 some type holds io, 4 every type at most
# 64 words), the index of the function to optimize (its original body; every other function
# has a body only when the run needs it) and a stage (0; 1.. stops after a phase, for the
# comparison with the TypeScript phases). Output words with code 0: the node count, per node
# op, operand count, callee, predicate, type, the operand pairs (node references renumbered to
# positions), then the ret pair and the literal iteration bound. Code 7: the functions whose
# body the run needs (to inline a call or unroll a fold, or to evaluate a call or a fold with
# literal operands, on the optimized body as src/optimize.ts does), then their count; the driver
# supplies them and everything they reach and repeats the run. Code 4: a limit (4096 nodes,
# 32768 operand slots, 256 stacked nodes) was reached; src/optimize.ts has none of these.
#
# The work is a sequence of phases on separate tables, since no state can hold them all:
# arena node table CL (a column per field, node ids are arena indices, AN = 4096), sequence SQ of
# the body's nodes, operand pairs OA (the input operand table, rewritten in place; new operand
# lists are appended after the input's), type facts TI. A phase decides (a fold over the nodes
# whose state is a table of per-node columns, one trip a node, each step a fold of 0 or 1 trips
# so that no function is larger than the chunk limits) and then materializes (one fold a
# table). Table reads are written out inline in the steps (a table passed to a call is copied by
# the C emitter); the macros `rdp`, `karg`, ... are expanded here by the generator.
#
# - expand (`edstep`): small pure scalar calls (INLINE_CALL_NODES 16) are inlined and folds of 1
#   to 8 literal trips unrolled (at most 256 body nodes, 2048 nodes in all, no io, at most 64
#   words a type): rename table RN, output sequence, instances (copies of a callee body).
# - pass (`passa`..`passd`): per node, in order, operands resolved through the substitutions;
#   a variable trip count that propagation would make a literal beyond the static compute bound
#   (2^24 trips times the callee's literal iterations) is kept as a `mov` of that literal;
#   effectful nodes (read write puts; call fold loop holding io) are kept and anchored;
#   constant evaluation (the evaluator below, on the optimized bodies, fuel as src/core.ts);
#   algebraic identities; reassociation of literal chains; strength reduction (div and rem by a
#   power of two); common-subexpression elimination (hash table, not arr rec; commutative ops
#   as a multiset); dead-code elimination from the ret and the anchored nodes.
# - forwardAggregates (`fwda`..`fwdo`) and up to eight more passes while it changes something.
# - schedule (`schstep`): the demand-driven order when nothing is effectful and no set/put
#   remains; literal iterations (`listep`); output (`ozwnode`).
#
# The evaluator (src/core.ts `exec`) is a machine with an explicit frame stack: `evstep`,
# charging 1 per function entry, 1 per node, 1 per fold/loop trip inside a body and
# max(1, length) for arr rec text set put; a call with literal operands runs on fuel 4096 (its
# exhaustion is a compile error in TypeScript: code 4), a fold/loop with at most 4096 trips on
# fuel 4096 * 64 (exhaustion keeps the node).
#
# compiler/optimize.a0 is generated from compiler/optimize.a0s by tools/a0s.ts (an expression
# language that compiles to one-node-per-line A0; see its header): edit the source, not this
# file.

use "emit_wasm.a0"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scalar operations (src/core.ts `evalOp` on u32 and bool, bools as 0/1): op p0 on p1 p2 p3.
# A0's own div/rem (a zero divisor gives all ones / the dividend) and shifts (low five bits)
# are evalOp's.

fn ozop u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
v2 add p1 p2
v3 sub p1 p2
v4 mul p1 p2
v5 and p1 p2
v6 or p1 p2
v7 xor p1 p2
v8 shl p1 p2
v9 shr p1 p2
v10 div p1 p2
v11 rem p1 p2
b12 eq p1 p2
b13 ne p1 p2
b14 lt p1 p2
b15 le p1 p2
b16 gt p1 p2
b17 ge p1 p2
v12 select b12 1 0
v13 select b13 1 0
v14 select b14 1 0
v15 select b15 1 0
v16 select b16 1 0
v17 select b17 1 0
c ne p1 0
v18 select c p2 p3
o2 eq p0 2
o3 eq p0 3
o4 eq p0 4
o5 eq p0 5
o6 eq p0 6
o7 eq p0 7
o8 eq p0 8
o9 eq p0 9
o10 eq p0 10
o11 eq p0 11
o12 eq p0 12
o13 eq p0 13
o14 eq p0 14
o15 eq p0 15
o16 eq p0 16
o17 eq p0 17
o18 eq p0 18
r2 select o2 v2 p1
r3 select o3 v3 r2
r4 select o4 v4 r3
r5 select o5 v5 r4
r6 select o6 v6 r5
r7 select o7 v7 r6
r8 select o8 v8 r7
r9 select o9 v9 r8
r10 select o10 v10 r9
r11 select o11 v11 r10
r12 select o12 v12 r11
r13 select o13 v13 r12
r14 select o14 v14 r13
r15 select o15 v15 r14
r16 select o16 v16 r15
r17 select o17 v17 r16
r18 select o18 v18 r17
ret r18
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The evaluator (src/core.ts `exec`). Machine table u32x128x512: scalars 0 status (0 running,
# 1 done, 2 fuel exhausted, 3 a capacity below is full, 4 an io operation), 1 fuel, 2 frames,
# 3 env top, 4 heap top, 5 result, 6 a frame has just returned (its value in 5), 7-14 the
# root (op, operand count, body or callee, predicate, trip, count, state, phase: 0 start,
# 1 awaiting the predicate, 2 the body, 3 the callee); 64-127 the root's operand values;
# frames from 128, 8 words each (function, env base, next node, phase: 0 idle, 1 awaiting
# the predicate, 2 the body, 3 the callee, 4 iterating; trip, count, state, parameter count),
# at most 1024 (the word above the top frame is scratch); env 8336-24703 (per frame its
# parameters, then its node values); heap 24704-65535: an array or record is a block (length,
# elements) and its value the block's index. Values are immutable, so blocks are shared.

# copy word p1 of a block or a parameter list to p3 + p1: mode p4 0 operand p5 + p1 of the
# frame with env base p6 and p7 parameters, 1 root operand p1, 2 word p8 + p1 (word p9 is p10);
# the first p13 words are p11, p12
fn evcp u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
pi add p5 p1
o_x mul pi 2
o_k_p shr o_x 7
o_k_g get p2 o_k_p
o_k_w and o_x 127
o_k get o_k_g o_k_w
o_w1 add o_k_w 1
o_v get o_k_g o_w1
o_r rec o_k o_v
o mov o_r
ok at o 0
ov at o 1
isn eq ok 1
s1 add p6 p7
s2 add s1 ov
s3 add p6 ov
os select isn s2 s3
os_p shr os 7
os_g get p0 os_p
os_w and os 127
om get os_g os_w
lit ge ok 3
opv select lit ov om
ri add 64 p1
ri_p shr ri 7
ri_g get p0 ri_p
ri_w and ri 127
rv get ri_g ri_w
bi add p8 p1
bi_p shr bi 7
bi_g get p0 bi_p
bi_w and bi 127
bv get bi_g bi_w
isr eq p1 p9
blk select isr p10 bv
m0 eq p4 0
m1 eq p4 1
v1 select m1 rv blk
v2 select m0 opv v1
spc lt p1 p13
k0 eq p1 0
xv select k0 p11 p12
val select spc xv v2
di add p3 p1
d_p shr di 7
d_g get p0 d_p
d_w and di 127
d_h set d_g d_w val
r set p0 d_p d_h
ret r
end
# root operand p1 from the list p2
fn evarg u32x128x512 u32 u32x64 -> u32x128x512
v get p2 p1
di add 64 p1
d_p shr di 7
d_g get p0 d_p
d_w and di 127
d_h set d_g d_w v
r set p0 d_p d_h
ret r
end
fn evgo u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 -> bool
s_g get p0 0
s get s_g 0
r eq s 0
ret r
end
# One machine step. Cases: a frame has returned (deliver its value to the top frame or the
# root), the root starts a call or a trip, or the top frame returns (its nodes are done),
# executes its next node, or starts its fold/loop's next trip. At most one frame is pushed
# (its parameters copied by the trailing `evcp` fold) or one block allocated per step.
fn evstep u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 -> u32x128x512
s0 get p0 0
fuel get s0 1
nfr get s0 2
etop get s0 3
htop get s0 4
res get s0 5
rtd get s0 6
rop get s0 7
rcal get s0 9
rprd get s0 10
ri get s0 11
rcnt get s0 12
rst get s0 13
rph get s0 14
hasf ne nfr 0
dm sub nfr 1
dd select hasf dm 0
d8 mul dd 8
fb add 128 d8
fb_p shr fb 7
fpg get p0 fb_p
fo and fb 127
fe get fpg fo
fo1 add fo 1
fbase get fpg fo1
fo2 add fo 2
fcur get fpg fo2
fo3 add fo 3
fph get fpg fo3
fo4 add fo 4
fi get fpg fo4
fo5 add fo 5
fcnt get fpg fo5
fo6 add fo 6
fst get fpg fo6
fo7 add fo 7
fnp get fpg fo7
fe7 mul fe 7
ffirst_w add fe7 4
ffirst_wp shr ffirst_w 7
ffirst_wg get p2 ffirst_wp
ffirst_wl and ffirst_w 127
ffirst_v get ffirst_wg ffirst_wl
ffirst mov ffirst_v
fnn_w add fe7 5
fnn_wp shr fnn_w 7
fnn_wg get p2 fnn_wp
fnn_wl and fnn_w 127
fnn_v get fnn_wg fnn_wl
fnn mov fnn_v
fret_w add fe7 6
fret_wp shr fret_w 7
fret_wg get p2 fret_wp
fret_wl and fret_w 127
fret_v get fret_wg fret_wl
fret mov fret_v
atend ge fcur fnn
gn add ffirst fcur
op_r6 mul gn 6
op_i add op_r6 1
op_v_p shr op_i 7
op_v_g get p3 op_v_p
op_v_w and op_i 127
op_v get op_v_g op_v_w
op mov op_v
na_r6 mul gn 6
na_i add na_r6 2
na_v_p shr na_i 7
na_v_g get p3 na_v_p
na_v_w and na_i 127
na_v get na_v_g na_v_w
na mov na_v
fa_r6 mul gn 6
fa_i add fa_r6 3
fa_v_p shr fa_i 7
fa_v_g get p3 fa_v_p
fa_v_w and fa_i 127
fa_v get fa_v_g fa_v_w
fa mov fa_v
cal_r6 mul gn 6
cal_i add cal_r6 4
cal_v_p shr cal_i 7
cal_v_g get p3 cal_v_p
cal_v_w and cal_i 127
cal_v get cal_v_g cal_v_w
cal mov cal_v
prd_r6 mul gn 6
prd_i add prd_r6 5
prd_v_p shr prd_i 7
prd_v_g get p3 prd_v_p
prd_v_w and prd_i 127
prd_v get prd_v_g prd_v_w
prd mov prd_v
vb add fbase fnp
# the values of operands 0 1 2 in the frame
ao_x mul fa 2
ao_k_p shr ao_x 7
ao_k_g get p4 ao_k_p
ao_k_w and ao_x 127
ao_k get ao_k_g ao_k_w
ao_w1 add ao_k_w 1
ao_v get ao_k_g ao_w1
ao_r rec ao_k ao_v
ao mov ao_r
ak at ao 0
aw at ao 1
an eq ak 1
as1 add vb aw
as2 add fbase aw
as select an as1 as2
as_p shr as 7
as_g get p0 as_p
as_w and as 127
am get as_g as_w
al ge ak 3
av select al aw am
fa1 add fa 1
bo_x mul fa1 2
bo_k_p shr bo_x 7
bo_k_g get p4 bo_k_p
bo_k_w and bo_x 127
bo_k get bo_k_g bo_k_w
bo_w1 add bo_k_w 1
bo_v get bo_k_g bo_w1
bo_r rec bo_k bo_v
bo mov bo_r
bk at bo 0
bw at bo 1
bn eq bk 1
bs1 add vb bw
bs2 add fbase bw
bs select bn bs1 bs2
bs_p shr bs 7
bs_g get p0 bs_p
bs_w and bs 127
bm get bs_g bs_w
bl ge bk 3
bv select bl bw bm
fa2 add fa 2
co_x mul fa2 2
co_k_p shr co_x 7
co_k_g get p4 co_k_p
co_k_w and co_x 127
co_k get co_k_g co_k_w
co_w1 add co_k_w 1
co_v get co_k_g co_w1
co_r rec co_k co_v
co mov co_r
ck at co 0
cw at co 1
cn eq ck 1
cs1 add vb cw
cs2 add fbase cw
cs select cn cs1 cs2
cs_p shr cs 7
cs_g get p0 cs_p
cs_w and cs 127
cm get cs_g cs_w
cl ge ck 3
cv select cl cw cm
# the value of the frame's ret operand (kind 5: the operand at args pair value)
rk0 shr fret 28
rv0 and fret 268435455
rk5 eq rk0 5
r5_x mul rv0 2
r5_k_p shr r5_x 7
r5_k_g get p4 r5_k_p
r5_k_w and r5_x 127
r5_k get r5_k_g r5_k_w
r5_w1 add r5_k_w 1
r5_v get r5_k_g r5_w1
r5_r rec r5_k r5_v
r5 mov r5_r
r5k at r5 0
r5v at r5 1
rk select rk5 r5k rk0
rvv select rk5 r5v rv0
rn eq rk 1
rs1 add vb rvv
rs2 add fbase rvv
rsl select rn rs1 rs2
rsl_p shr rsl 7
rsl_g get p0 rsl_p
rsl_w and rsl 127
rm get rsl_g rsl_w
rl ge rk 3
retf select rl rvv rm
# the node's value slot
sl add vb fcur
sl_p shr sl 7
sl_g get p0 sl_p
sl_w and sl 127
slo get sl_g sl_w
# the block of operand 0 (get at set put): its length and the element read
bl_p shr av 7
bl_g get p0 bl_p
bl_w and av 127
blen get bl_g bl_w
gidx rem bv blen
isget eq op 25
isset eq op 26
eidx select isget gidx bv
jidx select isset gidx bv
ea1 add av 1
ea add ea1 eidx
ea_p shr ea 7
ea_g get p0 ea_p
ea_w and ea 127
gv get ea_g ea_w
# the case
rt ne rtd 0
nrt select rt false true
nhf select hasf false true
isa and rt hasf
isb and rt nhf
isc and nrt nhf
isd and nrt hasf
nae select atend false true
isd1 and isd atend
isdn and isd nae
ph0 eq fph 0
ph4 eq fph 4
isd2 and isdn ph0
isd3 and isdn ph4
iscall eq op 19
isfo eq op 20
islp eq op 21
isfl or isfo islp
o22 eq op 22
o23 eq op 23
o24 eq op 24
agg1 or o22 o23
isagg or agg1 o24
isput eq op 28
isup or isset isput
isio ge op 29
issc le op 18
isnew or isagg isup
pv0 call ozop op av bv cv
pv1 select issc pv0 gv
pv select isnew htop pv1
np1 or iscall isfl
np2 or np1 isio
plain select np2 false true
d2p and isd2 plain
d2c and isd2 iscall
d2f and isd2 isfl
d2io and isd2 isio
more lt fi fcnt
nmore select more false true
d3m and isd3 more
d3e and isd3 nmore
fph1 eq fph 1
fph2 eq fph 2
fph3 eq fph 3
rtrue eq res 1
nrtrue select rtrue false true
a3 and isa fph3
a1 and isa fph1
a1t and a1 rtrue
a1f and a1 nrtrue
a2 and isa fph2
rph1 eq rph 1
rph2 eq rph 2
rph3 eq rph 3
b3 and isb rph3
b1 and isb rph1
b1t and b1 rtrue
b1f and b1 nrtrue
b2 and isb rph2
rcall eq rop 19
rlp eq rop 21
nrcall select rcall false true
rmore lt ri rcnt
nrmore select rmore false true
c1 and isc rcall
cfl and isc nrcall
c2 and cfl rmore
c3 and cfl nrmore
# the pushed frame: from the top frame (its node's operands) or from the root
pf1 or d2c d3m
pframe or pf1 a1t
pr1 or b1t c1
proot or pr1 c2
push or pframe proot
ed3 select islp prd cal
ef1 select d3m ed3 cal
ec2 select rlp rprd rcal
er1 select c2 ec2 rcal
pe select pframe ef1 er1
pe7 mul pe 7
pnp_w add pe7 1
pnp_wp shr pnp_w 7
pnp_wg get p2 pnp_wp
pnp_wl and pnp_w 127
pnp_v get pnp_wg pnp_wl
pnp mov pnp_v
pnn_w add pe7 5
pnn_wp shr pnn_w 7
pnn_wg get p2 pnn_wp
pnn_wl and pnn_w 127
pnn_v get pnn_wg pnn_wl
pnn mov pnn_v
nsp0 or d2c c1
pnsp select nsp0 0 2
px0 select pframe fst rst
px1 select pframe fi ri
# fuel: the node, a callee's entry, a trip and its entry, the copy of an aggregate
lenc select isup blen 0
nac select isagg na 0
cc select iscall 1 0
u2a add 1 cc
u2b add u2a nac
u2 add u2b lenc
ud2 select isd2 u2 0
ud3 select d3m 2 0
up1 or a1t b1t
up2 or up1 c1
up3 or up2 c2
ua select up3 1 0
u1 add ud2 ud3
u add u1 ua
exh gt u fuel
fuel2 sub fuel u
# capacities: 1024 frames, the env, the heap
pfull ge nfr 1024
ptop1 add etop pnp
ptop add ptop1 pnn
pover gt ptop 24704
pc1 or pfull pover
pcap and push pc1
alloc and isd2 isnew
ncnt select isagg na blen
ncopy add ncnt 1
htop2 add htop ncopy
aover gt htop2 65536
acap and alloc aover
cap or pcap acap
dn1 or b3 b1f
done or dn1 c3
st1 select done 1 0
st2 select d2io 4 st1
st3 select cap 3 st2
st4 select exh 2 st3
ok1 or exh cap
ok select ok1 false true
# the top frame
av1 or d2p d3e
av2 or av1 a3
adv or av2 a1f
cur1 add fcur 1
cur2 select adv cur1 fcur
ph1a select islp 1 2
phx1 select a2 4 fph
phx2 select a1f 0 phx1
phx3 select a1t 2 phx2
phx4 select a3 0 phx3
phx5 select d3e 0 phx4
phx6 select d3m ph1a phx5
phx7 select d2f 4 phx6
phx8 select d2c 3 phx7
fi1 add fi 1
fix1 select a2 fi1 fi
fix2 select d2f 0 fix1
cnt2 select d2f av fcnt
stx1 select a2 res fst
stx2 select d2f bv stx1
sv1 select a3 res fst
slv select d2p pv sv1
slx select adv slv slo
# the root and the scalars
nfr1 add nfr 1
nfr2 sub nfr 1
nfx1 select isd1 nfr2 nfr
nfx2 select push nfr1 nfx1
etx1 select isd1 fbase etop
etx2 select push ptop etx1
htx select alloc htop2 htop
rr1 or b1f c3
rsx1 select rr1 rst res
rsx2 select isd1 retf rsx1
rab or isa isb
rtx1 select rab 0 rtd
rtx2 select isd1 1 rtx1
ri1 add ri 1
rix select b2 ri1 ri
rstx select b2 res rst
rpc select rlp 1 2
rpx1 select b2 0 rph
rpx2 select b1t 2 rpx1
rpx3 select c2 rpc rpx2
rpx4 select c1 3 rpx3
# writes: the slot, the top frame, the pushed frame (above the top: scratch when none), the
# scalars (page 0 rewritten from its value on entry)
sl_h set sl_g sl_w slx
t1 set p0 sl_p sl_h
tf_g get t1 fb_p
tf1 set tf_g fo2 cur2
tf2 set tf1 fo3 phx8
tf3 set tf2 fo4 fix2
tf4 set tf3 fo5 cnt2
tf5 set tf4 fo6 stx2
t2 set t1 fb_p tf5
n8 mul nfr 8
nb add 128 n8
nb_p shr nb 7
nb_o and nb 127
nf_g get t2 nb_p
nf1 set nf_g nb_o pe
nb1 add nb_o 1
nf2 set nf1 nb1 etop
nb2 add nb_o 2
nf3 set nf2 nb2 0
nb3 add nb_o 3
nf4 set nf3 nb3 0
nb4 add nb_o 4
nf5 set nf4 nb4 0
nb5 add nb_o 5
nf6 set nf5 nb5 0
nb6 add nb_o 6
nf7 set nf6 nb6 0
nb7 add nb_o 7
nf8 set nf7 nb7 pnp
t3 set t2 nb_p nf8
g1 set s0 0 st4
g2 set g1 1 fuel2
g3 set g2 2 nfx2
g4 set g3 3 etx2
g5 set g4 4 htx
g6 set g5 5 rsx2
g7 set g6 6 rtx2
g8 set g7 11 rix
g9 set g8 13 rstx
g10 set g9 14 rpx4
t4 set t3 0 g10
# the copy: the pushed frame's parameters, or the new block (arr rec text: the operand
# count, then the operands; set put: the old block with the element replaced)
pc select push pnp ncopy
pa select alloc ncopy 0
nc0 select push pc pa
nc select ok nc0 0
dst select push etop htop
md1 select pframe 0 1
md2 select isagg 0 2
md select alloc md2 md1
fam sub fa 1
aga and alloc isagg
fa3 select aga fam fa
ns1 select isagg 1 0
ns select alloc ns1 pnsp
x0 select alloc na px0
j1 add jidx 1
t5 fold evcp nc t4 p4 dst md fa3 fbase fnp av j1 cv x0 px1 ns
ret t5
end
# Evaluate op p4 (19 call, 20 fold, 21 loop) of the eval function p5 (predicate p6) on the p7
# literal operands p3 with fuel p8: (status, value), status 1 done, 2 fuel exhausted, 3 a
# capacity is full, 4 an io operation
fn evrun u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x64 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> (u32,u32)
z call z512
c0 get p3 0
c1 get p3 1
s0 get z 0
s1 set s0 1 p8
s2 set s1 3 8336
s3 set s2 4 24704
